  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "Suppose $a$ and $b$ are positive and that $a\\ne1$ and $b\\ne1$. Prove that\n$$\\log_a b-\\log_b a=\\log_a(ab)\\log_b\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\log_a b-\\log_b a=\\log_a(ab)\\log_b\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right)$.\n\nUse base swapping, factorise the difference of squares, then apply the product, quotient and change-of-base laws.",
      "worked": "By base swapping and the logarithm laws,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\log_a b-\\frac{1}{\\log_a b}\\\\\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\frac{(\\log_a b)^2-1}{\\log_a b}\\\\\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\frac{(\\log_a b-1)(\\log_a b+1)}{\\log_a b}\\\\\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\frac{(\\log_a b-\\log_a a)(\\log_a b+\\log_a a)}{\\log_a b}\\\\\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\frac{\\log_a(b/a)\\log_a(ab)}{\\log_a b}\\\\\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\log_a(ab)\\frac{\\log_a(b/a)}{\\log_a b}\\\\\n\\log_a b-\\log_b a&=\\log_a(ab)\\log_b\\left(\\frac{b}{a}\\right).\n\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 76
  },
